<section class="fees-section" id="fees"><div class="seller-wrap narrow-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Clear from the first order</p><h2>Fees you can understand.</h2><p>We keep the seller experience straightforward. You see the service fee before an order is accepted, and your payout is available after the order is complete.</p></div><div class="seller-wrap fee-grid"><article class="fee-card"><div class="fee-icon">%</div><h3>Marketplace service fee</h3><p>A percentage of the cake subtotal that supports ordering, discovery, and seller tools.</p><strong>From 7%</strong><small>Rates shown are illustrative and subject to your seller agreement.</small></article><article class="fee-card"><div class="fee-icon">↗</div><h3>Payment processing</h3><p>A per-order fee for securely processing your customer’s payment.</p><strong>2.9% + KES 30</strong><small>Calculated on the order total at checkout.</small></article><article class="fee-card"><div class="fee-icon">♥</div><h3>Your delivery, your choice</h3><p>Set collection, delivery, and delivery-zone options that work for your kitchen.</p><strong>You stay in control</strong><small>Delivery charges are shown separately to customers.</small></article></div></section>

<section class="calculator-section"><div class="seller-wrap calculator-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Grow with every order</p><h2>Your monthly sales can unlock better rates.</h2><p>Enter an estimate to see an example of how a volume-based seller rate could work for your bakery.</p></div><div class="rate-calculator"><label for="sales">Estimated monthly cake sales <output id="sales-output">KES 50,000</output></label><input id="sales" type="range" min="10000" max="500000" value="50000" step="5000" /><div class="rate-result"><span>Your illustrative service rate</span><strong id="rate-output">7%</strong><small id="tier-output">Starting baker tier</small></div><div class="rate-scale"><span>KES 10k</span><span>KES 500k+</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="seller-wrap payout-section"><div class="payout-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A payout that makes sense</p><h2>Only pay a service fee on the cake itself.</h2><p>Delivery and applicable taxes are kept separate, so your marketplace service fee is based on the price of what you baked.</p></div><div class="payout-example"><div class="payout-row"><span>Celebration cake</span><strong>KES 4,000</strong></div><div class="payout-row muted"><span>Delivery</span><strong>Separate</strong></div><div class="payout-row muted"><span>Applicable taxes</span><strong>Separate</strong></div><div class="payout-row total"><span>Service-fee base</span><strong>KES 4,000</strong></div><p>Example only. Your actual rate and payout depend on your seller agreement and completed order details.</p></div></section>

<section class="faq-section"><div class="seller-wrap faq-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions, answered</p><h2>Seller FAQ</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details open><summary>How do I apply to become a Rumy Cakes seller?</summary><p>Start with the short application below. We’ll review your bakery details and follow up with the next steps.</p></details><details><summary>When do I receive my payout?</summary><p>Payout timing and requirements are confirmed as part of your seller onboarding and agreement.</p></details><details><summary>Can I offer collection and delivery?</summary><p>Yes. You can set the fulfilment options and service area that suit your bakery.</p></details><details><summary>Are fees the same for every baker?</summary><p>Rates may vary based on your seller agreement, location, and monthly sales volume. We’ll always make your applicable rate clear.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="apply-section" id="apply"><div class="seller-wrap apply-card"><p class="eyebrow">Ready when you are</p><h2>Bring your bakery to Rumy Cakes.</h2><p>Share your cakes with more people and make every order feel personal.</p><a class="seller-button light" href="mailto:hello@rumycakes.com?subject=Rumy%20Cakes%20seller%20application">Start your application</a></div></section>

<script>
  const sales = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#sales');
  const salesOutput = document.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>('#sales-output');
  const rateOutput = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#rate-output');
  const tierOutput = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#tier-output');
  const updateRate = () => { if (!sales || !salesOutput || !rateOutput || !tierOutput) return; const value = Number(sales.value); const rate = value >= 300000 ? 5 : value >= 150000 ? 6 : 7; salesOutput.value = `KES ${value.toLocaleString('en-KE')}`; rateOutput.textContent = `${rate}%`; tierOutput.textContent = rate === 5 ? 'Established bakery tier' : rate === 6 ? 'Growing bakery tier' : 'Starting baker tier'; };
  sales?.addEventListener('input', updateRate); updateRate();
</script>
